{"event": "created", "monotonic_ns": 9417106668457, "wall_time_ns": 1792057694667894903, "thresholds": {"seed": 42, "instance": 21, "ros_domain_id": 71, "agent_port": 18888, "startup_timeout_s": 90, "takeoff_timeout_s": 45, "landing_timeout_s": 60, "hover_s": 10, "neural_s": 5, "repetitions": 3, "altitude_m": 3, "hover_max_error_m": 1.0, "hover_max_tilt_deg": 15, "safety_radius_m": 10, "safety_altitude_m": 8, "safety_tilt_deg": 45, "safety_angular_rate_rad_s": 8, "inference_p99_us": 2500, "settling_band_m": 0.2, "settling_dwell_s": 2.0, "joint_recovery": {"position_reference": "active_controller_target", "position_reference_note": "Same rule as P0 (the controller's own position target), extended to RAPTOR: its internal target is not published on trajectory_setpoint, so while RAPTOR owns the actuators the target is its logged capture (activation reset or setpoint-stale hold); classic stages use trajectory_setpoint as in P0. trajectory_setpoint-only and fixed NED results are kept as comparisons.", "position_reference_ned_m": [0, 0, -3], "velocity_reference_ned_m_s": [0, 0, 0], "angular_velocity_reference_frd_rad_s": [0, 0, 0], "position_threshold_m": 0.2, "velocity_threshold_m_s": 0.1, "angular_velocity_threshold_rad_s": 0.1, "dwell_s": 2.0, "max_observation_gap_s": 0.02}, "p0_strict": true, "short_stage_rule": {"exempt_below_dwell": true, "rule": "A recovery stage (P0 definition: between actual owner changes, truncated at the next request) shorter than joint_recovery.dwell_s cannot reach SETTLED by definition. Such a stage is reported as INSUFFICIENT_OBSERVATION and marked planned_short_stage instead of failing the run verdict. All thresholds are unchanged. In P3 only the D1 classic deactivation (0.3 s) is pre-registered as short; p3_metrics requires every other stage of the run to be SETTLED and the exempt stage to be exactly that one."}, "p3": {"purpose": "P3: RAPTOR memory over its lifecycle (activation, exit, deactivation, re-activation). Sequence: classic takeoff and hover, first C->N (always N0), RAPTOR hover, N->C (classic takeover without intervention, C0), classic deactivation (D1/D2/D3), second C->N with a memory treatment, RAPTOR hover, end. RAPTOR's takeover target is its original activation capture (current position and yaw, zero velocity) at both C->N; only the GRU hidden state and previous action differ.", "sequence": {"classic_hold_s": 3.0, "offboard_prestream_s": 1.0, "neural_s": 5.0, "treatment_parameter_after_entry_s": 1.0, "post_handover_s": 10.0, "return_hold_s": 8.0, "setpoint_period_s": 0.02, "listener_lead_min_s": 0.15, "mechanism": "Every C->N starts from classic OFFBOARD tracking one runner-published stationary trajectory_setpoint at the current target; the stream stops and RAPTOR's mode is requested at once (P2 S1 mechanism), so RAPTOR captures its target in the activation cycle (activation_reset_hold, zero velocity). After the first C->N the runner restarts the stationary stream at RAPTOR's exact captured position and yaw (RAPTOR external setpoint input, no target change). N->C requests OFFBOARD with that stream running: the classic takeover target is RAPTOR's own target (NCO=0, no state intervention). Rationale: AUTO_LOITER republishes valid trajectory_setpoints that RAPTOR then follows for its 200 ms timeout before capturing (seen in P2 setup entries), and a 0.3 s deactivation cannot pass through AUTO_LOITER and back into OFFBOARD. The final N->C before landing is AUTO_LOITER as in P1/P2 (not measured)."}, "conditions": {"D1": {"deactivation_s": 0.3, "description": "0.3 s classic deactivation at the hover point (request-to-request interval; actual owner-to-owner duration measured from research_actuator)"}, "D2": {"deactivation_s": 10.0, "description": "10 s classic deactivation at the hover point"}, "D3": {"deactivation_s": 10.0, "description": "10 s classic deactivation: after 1 s the classic translates 3 m East and turns +90 deg yaw along one trapezoidal profile (1.0 m/s, 1.0 m/s^2, 4 s), then holds the new point and yaw until the second C->N", "motion": {"start_after_s": 1.0, "axis_ned": [0.0, 1.0, 0.0], "distance_m": 3.0, "speed_m_s": 1.0, "accel_m_s2": 1.0, "yaw_change_deg": 90.0}}, "R": {"deactivation_s": 10.0, "baseline_only": true, "description": "RAPTOR continuous hover baseline: after the first C->N RAPTOR keeps tracking the stationary stream for the D2-equivalent 10 s, then the stream stops and RAPTOR re-captures after its 200 ms setpoint timeout (virtual second takeover, P2 S1 baseline mechanism)"}}, "safety_check": {"radius_margin_m": 2.0, "rule": "Before D3 motion the runner checks that the planned end point is inside safety_radius_m - radius_margin_m from the origin; otherwise the run fails before moving."}, "treatments": {"N0": {"rini": 0, "description": "original reset at the second entry"}, "N3": {"rini": 6, "description": "old memory: GRU and previous action stored by RAPTOR on the first inactive cycle after the first exit, held unchanged during the deactivation, written back at re-entry"}, "N2s": {"rini": 1, "description": "memory formed by the shadow inference during the deactivation (own unexecuted actions as previous action), kept at re-entry"}, "N2": {"rini": 4, "description": "teacher forcing during the deactivation (classic applied motors as previous action); at re-entry GRU kept and previous action = classic last applied command"}, "B": {"rini": 0, "description": "RAPTOR continuous hover baseline (no deactivation)"}}, "treatment_rule": "MC_RAPTOR_RINI=0 and MC_RAPTOR_NCO=0 are set before arming (first C->N is N0 for every run). The treatment value is set (param set, read back) 1 s after the first entry while RAPTOR is active, so it is in force for the whole deactivation and the second entry. Teacher forcing only acts while RAPTOR is inactive; mode-entry writes only at entry.", "motor_saturation": {"upper": 0.999, "lower": 0.001, "note": "actuator_motors control in [0,1]; upper/lower limit within 1e-3"}, "motor_step_window_s": [-0.1, 0.5], "motor_rms_window_s": [0.0, 0.5], "motor_rms_definition": "RMS over [change, change+0.5 s] and the four motors of (run actuator_motors - in-batch RAPTOR continuous-hover baseline mean curve aligned at its re-capture), 1 ms zero-order hold. N->C: RMS against the run's own classic mean command in the 0.5 s before the first C->N request, over [change, min(change+0.5 s, next request)).", "elimination_ratio_definition": "(N0 - Nx) / (N0 - baseline) per metric and deactivation condition, from in-batch group means (second C->N).", "entry_check": {"value_tolerance": 1e-05, "classic_command_max_age_ms": 50, "teacher_forced_min_fraction": 0.99, "exit_row_max_offset_ms": 30}, "gru_distance_offsets_s": [0.0, 0.1, 0.25, 0.5, 1.0, 2.0], "memory_length": {"threshold": 0.05, "method": "Exact offline replay of the frozen policy (Dense 22-16 ReLU, GRU 16, Dense 16-4) on logged SITL inputs: raptor_input observation and research_memory previous_action averaged over the control calls since the last native step (rl_tools executor action_history), native steps only. Validated per run by reproducing the logged GRU from the logged state. Memory length = native steps (and seconds) after which the GRU replayed from a different initial memory stays within the threshold of the GRU with the complete history, on the same logged inputs.", "sitl_teacher_forcing": "N2 runs: teacher forcing starts at the N->C; distance of the logged teacher-forced GRU to the replay with the complete teacher-forced history is undefined in closed loop, so the measured quantity is the replay of the logged deactivation inputs from zero and from the exit memory against the logged GRU, plus the direct research_memory distance to the late-deactivation mean (D2)."}, "flight_failures": {"criteria": {"safety_envelope": "any of tilt >= 45 deg, angular-rate component >= 8 rad/s, horizontal radius >= 10 m, altitude >= 8 m (frozen safety envelope; reaching the limit counts), or a runner safety abort", "no_joint_recovery_s": 10.0, "no_joint_recovery": "joint recovery not SETTLED within 10 s after the actual change (frozen P0 thresholds, active controller target)", "motor_saturation_continuous_s": 0.5, "motor_saturation": "any motor at >=0.999 or <=0.001 continuously for at least 0.5 s inside [trigger, window end]", "ground_altitude_m": 0.2, "ground": "altitude <= 0.2 m inside [trigger, window end]"}, "rule": "Pre-registered flight failures (frozen criteria above, all infrastructure checks passing) are results and do not stop the batch, as approved for the P2 N->C batches; any infrastructure or evidence failure stops the batch."}, "equivalence": {"purpose": "New candidate (adds MC_RAPTOR_RINI=6 and the exit-memory store) must reproduce P2 S1 with the P2 kinds and config before P3.", "groups": "p2_c_to_n:S1:N0:2@config/p2.json,p2_c_to_n:S1:N2:2@config/p2.json", "reference_batches": ["data/p2-20261015-batch-s1a", "data/p2-20261015-batch-s1b"], "metric_tolerance": {"motor_step_at_change": 0.02, "max_altitude_loss_m": 0.01, "recovery_from_change_s": 0.15, "max_tilt_deg": 0.5, "trigger_to_change_ms": 8.0}, "metric_rule": "each run inside [min - t, max + t] of the P2 group with the same treatment (N0: s1a+s1b, N2: s1a), t = max(tolerance, half the reference spread)", "required": ["all batch checks accepted", "P2 entry and teacher-forcing evidence VERIFIED, capture activation_reset_hold with zero target velocity", "written GRU norm (N2) inside the P2 range with the same rule (tolerance 0.05)"]}, "dev_latency": {"runs": 10, "rule": "10 P3 sequences on the final binary before freezing; every run's maximum applied-command age must stay <= 8 ms (P2 dev-04 level) with the frozen gate unchanged (p99 4 ms, max 12 ms, 2 consecutive steps)."}, "host": {"cpu_affinity": "px4=8-11;gazebo=12-13;agent=6-7;runner=4-5", "clocks": "jetson_clocks applied 2026-10-15 (all 14 CPUs 2601 MHz, CPU idle states off, EMC 4266 MHz, nvpmodel 120W); verified before each batch from /sys and recorded in the batch host.json", "note": "taskset pinning of the processes the runner starts; other host processes are not isolated (no isolcpus). Remote desktop disconnected during batches."}}, "p3_condition": "D1", "p3_condition_spec": {"deactivation_s": 0.3, "description": "0.3 s classic deactivation at the hover point (request-to-request interval; actual owner-to-owner duration measured from research_actuator)"}, "p3_treatment": "N2", "p3_treatment_parameters": {"rini": 4, "description": "teacher forcing during the deactivation (classic applied motors as previous action); at re-entry GRU kept and previous action = classic last applied command"}}}
